# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: pass the charon-driver options in a temporary file (CHARON_ARGS_FILE), not the environment
#
# Large option sets (the patterns of --opaque-file, --start-from-file and --opaque-hard-file)
# exceeded ARG_MAX when serialized into CHARON_ARGS and CHARON_OPAQUE_HARD, so spawning cargo or
# charon-driver failed with ArgumentListTooLong. charon now writes the serialized options and the
# --opaque-hard patterns to a fresh temporary file, removed once the child exits, and passes its
# path in CHARON_ARGS_FILE; charon-driver fails on a missing, unreadable or malformed file. The
# serialized options (which the llbc records) are unchanged.

